Ambient TV: preserve signed CNN feature texture reads on GLES.

Anime4K stores learned features in RGBA16F targets. NVIDIA GLES can corrupt
low-precision sampling/arithmetic on these textures even though the render
target is floating point (mpv-player/mpv#18566). Use highp sampler2D wherever
fragment highp is supported; retain mediump for GLES 2 devices without it.
sampler3D and samplerExternalOES are unchanged.

Reference: https://github.com/mpv-player/mpv/issues/18566

diff --git a/video/out/gpu/shader_cache.c b/video/out/gpu/shader_cache.c
--- a/video/out/gpu/shader_cache.c
+++ b/video/out/gpu/shader_cache.c
@@ -788,7 +788,14 @@ static void gl_sc_generate(struct gl_shader_cache *sc,
         ADD(header, "precision mediump float;\n");
         ADD(header, "#endif\n");
 
+        // Signed CNN feature maps need high-precision reads as well as FP16
+        // storage. NVIDIA GLES can otherwise corrupt small-weight arithmetic.
+        // Preserve the fallback for GLES 2 implementations without highp.
+        ADD(header, "#if __VERSION__ >= 300 || defined(GL_FRAGMENT_PRECISION_HIGH)\n");
+        ADD(header, "precision highp sampler2D;\n");
+        ADD(header, "#else\n");
         ADD(header, "precision mediump sampler2D;\n");
+        ADD(header, "#endif\n");
         if (sc->ra->caps & RA_CAP_TEX_3D)
             ADD(header, "precision mediump sampler3D;\n");
     }
